Negative control for the tri-state CLEAR path (P1-R7).

Drops the unset guard from `onPick`, so clearing resolves through `find` on a
nil value — which lodash matches against the FIRST option, silently setting the
filter it was asked to clear. Any assertion that reads the WIRE (the cleared
`eq` leaf is absent) goes red; one that only reads the control's own pressed
state stays green, which is the point.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

diff --git a/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/FilterRenderer.vue b/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/FilterRenderer.vue
--- a/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/FilterRenderer.vue
+++ b/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/FilterRenderer.vue
@@ -381,9 +381,7 @@
 
   write(
     RequestFilterOperator.EQUAL,
-    isNil(picked) || picked === FILTER_UNSET_VALUE
-      ? undefined
-      : get(find(options.value, { value: picked }), "const")
+    get(find(options.value, { value: picked }), "const")
   );
 }
 
